course: dictionary
lesson: 16094
title: Watering: one word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Watering comes from the word water, and it can do different jobs in a sentence. Look at the words around it to find out which job it is doing. «Sam is watering the tomato plants.» Here watering is a verb, an action: Sam is giving water to the plants.
explain: «The garden needs watering in the hot summer.» Here watering is a noun, a thing that happens. Ask yourself: is somebody doing an action, is it a thing, or is it describing something? That tells you which job the word is doing.
explain: «Her watering eyes stung from the smoke.» Here watering is an adjective. It describes the eyes and means the eyes are filling with water. «The mouth-watering smell of bread filled the kitchen» works the same way: the smell makes your mouth fill with water.
fact: Watering means giving water to plants or animals.
fact: A «watering can» is a container with a spout, used for watering plants.
fact: A «watering hole» is a pool where animals drink.
fact: «Mouth-watering» means so tempting or good-smelling that your mouth fills with water.
fact: Plants need watering, light and warmth to grow.
exercise: «The gardener is watering the roses.» What is watering doing in this sentence? | Making the roses fill with tears | Stopping the roses from growing | *Giving water to the roses | Digging a hole for the roses
exercise: «We filled the watering can at the tap.» What is a watering can? | A bucket for sand | A small pond for fish | A hose for washing cars | *A container with a spout for watering plants
exercise: «The lions came to the watering hole at dusk.» What is a watering hole? | A hole in the road | *A pool where animals drink | A tap in the garden | A small hole dug for plants
test: In «Her watering eyes stung from the smoke», what kind of word is watering? | Verb | *Adjective | Noun
test: «The bakery smelled mouth-watering.» What does mouth-watering mean? | Smelling bad | *Smelling so good that your mouth fills with water | Smelling of smoke | Smelling of water
exam: In «Sam ran to fill the watering can so he could keep watering the tomatoes», what does watering mean? | A pool where animals drink | Making eyes fill with tears | *Giving water to plants | Dripping from a tap
